    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Here, on both cheeks and the nose. It is... how to say, it is red like I am blushing always. And sometimes on the forehead also.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:24",
      "end_timestamp": "00:38",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Red cheeks and nose, since two years. Does the redness stay all day, or does it come in waves?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:40",
      "end_timestamp": "00:50",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Waves, mostly. It becomes too much when I drink hot tea or when I eat spicy food. Then my face is... flushing, flushing like a heater.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:52",
      "end_timestamp": "01:05",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Sun, also. And in the kitchen, when I am standing near the stove.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:15",
      "end_timestamp": "01:21",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Sun and heat. Is there any pain with it, or a burning feeling?",
